# Ansible
*.retry
# Every real inventory is host-specific configuration and must never be committed.
# `!ansible/inventory/example/` alone does NOT work here - it only re-includes the
# directory entry, not files inside it that a more specific pattern already excludes
# (a documented git gitignore limitation, confirmed 2026-08-14: it silently kept
# ansible/inventory/example/ untracked in this repo since the initial commit - nobody
# who cloned it ever got the example inventory the README's quick start depends on).
# Ignoring everything under ansible/inventory/ and re-including example/ plus its full
# recursive contents sidesteps that trap entirely.
ansible/inventory/*
!ansible/inventory/example/
!ansible/inventory/example/**
*.vault
.vault_pass
vault_password_file

# Environment files
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Vagrant
.vagrant/
*.box

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Secrets - never commit these
*_password
*_secret
*_token
*_key
# Docker secret files are created locally at runtime (docker/<stack>/secrets/) and hold
# plain-text credentials - the whole directory stays out of the repo.
docker/*/secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Local tooling settings. Machine-specific and not shareable: this file records
# per-machine grants that can include internal hostnames and local scratch paths. It was
# only kept out of the repo by a *global* gitignore in the maintainer's home directory
# (~/.config/git/ignore) - that protects one machine and does not travel with a clone,
# so a `git add -A` on any other checkout would have committed it. Ignored here so the
# protection ships with the repository (found while auditing for publication, #50).
# Deliberately only settings.local.json: a shared settings.json is committable.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# MkDocs
site/

# Logs
*.log

# Local-only redirect stub. The real, public content lives in CONVENTIONS.md (renamed
# 2026-08-19) - kept out of the public repo deliberately, not left off as an oversight.
# Some local tooling auto-loads a file of exactly this name; the stub points such tooling
# at CONVENTIONS.md so per-machine auto-loading keeps working without the stub itself
# ever being committed.
CLAUDE.md
